            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A patient, long before becoming the subject of medical scrutiny is, at first simply a storyteller, a narrator of suffering-a traveler who has visited the kingdom of the ill. &quot;To relieve an illness one must begin, then, by understanding the story.&quot; The Emperor of All Maladies; Siddhartha Mukherjee.</AbstractText>
